GATE 4.1 -- is blur-per-step in pixels really aperture-invariant?
==============================================================================
  Policy: step the focus axis so each step grows the CoC by 1.0 px.
 marked   N_eff  step (um obj)  CoC/step (px)  DOF-ish (um)  frames for 600um
    4.0    12.0         15.360         1.0000        15.360                40
    5.6    16.8         21.504         1.0000        21.504                28
    8.0    24.0         30.720         1.0000        30.720                20
   11.0    33.0         42.240         1.0000        42.240                15
   16.0    48.0         61.440         1.0000        61.440                10
  -> step_um is proportional to N_eff and CoC/step is EXACTLY constant.
     The invariance holds, but it is a CONSEQUENCE OF THE SAMPLING POLICY
     (step proportional to DOF), not a free-standing property of the optics.
     Physical content: frames ~ 1/N_eff at fixed depth. That part is real.

